# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 268-270 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, RUN 2, 2026-09-26): the three acquisitions — money, intercourse,
# the document by the compare (268); THE SCHOOLS ON THE GROUNDS OF DIVORCE, the bill for her name, the inks and the leaves, the cutting off and R. Eliezer's
# condition answered by four elders, her hand and her domain, the thrown bill (269 — HEADLESS inside 24:1, FOURTEEN rows, the walk's largest headless piska,
# read whole from the export); she goes out, the other man, the hater and the burier, the widow and the divorcee before the levir, the levirate bill, the
# husband from over the sea, betrothal and marriage, the sotah, Jeremiah's receipt, the child no abomination, the court warned (270). Every row READ WHOLE in
# both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(268, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN A MAN TAKES A WIFE AND HAS HER" (24:1) — THE WOMAN IS ACQUIRED BY MONEY; THE HEBREW SLAVE-GIRL WOULD ARGUE IT, THE LEVIRATE WIDOW REFUTES IT — "TAKES" TEACHES IT. The head row of piska 268 — the edge clean (267:4 stopped at 23:26) ({SP_(268, 1, "שהאשה", "נקנית", "בכסף")} "the woman is acquired by money"; {SP_(268, 1, "אמה", "העבריה")} "the Hebrew slave-girl"; {SP_(268, 1, "יבמה", "תוכיח")} "the levirate widow proves it"): THE FIRST OF KIDDUSHIN 1:1\'S THREE MODES read out of the divorce verse (the English\'s "cf.") — the marriage the state the bill dissolves (the design\'s DV24-01). Fresh.')
srow(268, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HAS HER" — ACQUIRED BY INTERCOURSE; THE LEVIRATE WIDOW WOULD ARGUE IT, THE SLAVE-GIRL REFUTES IT — "HAS HER" TEACHES IT. ({SP_(268, 2, "שהאשה", "נקנית", "בבעילה")} "the woman is acquired by intercourse"; {SP_(268, 2, "אמה", "העבריה", "תוכיח")} "the Hebrew slave-girl proves it"): the second mode — the two foils swapped, the same shape mirrored (268:1). Fresh.')
srow(268, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE ALSO BY A DOCUMENT? THE ARGUMENT FROM MONEY FAILS (MONEY BUYS CONSECRATED THINGS, A DOCUMENT DOES NOT); THE TEACHING: "HE WRITES HER A BILL … AND SHE GOES OUT AND BECOMES ANOTHER\'S" — HER BECOMING COMPARED TO HER GOING OUT: AS THE GOING OUT BY A DOCUMENT, SO THE BECOMING. ({SP_(268, 3, "מנין", "אף", "בשטר")} "whence also by a document?"; {SP_(268, 3, "מקיש", "הויתה", "לזה", "ליציאתה", "מזה")} "it compares her becoming this one\'s to her going out from that one"): THE COMPARE (hekesh) of 24:1-2 — the bill of marriage from the bill of divorce; the third mode; Kiddushin 1:1 complete in three rows. Fresh.')
srow(269, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF SHE FINDS NO FAVOR IN HIS EYES" — HENCE THE SCHOOL OF SHAMMAI: A MAN DIVORCES HIS WIFE ONLY IF HE FOUND LEWDNESS IN HER, "AN UNSEEMLY THING"; THE SCHOOL OF HILLEL: EVEN IF SHE BURNT HIS DISH, "A THING". The head row of the HEADLESS piska 269 (inside 24:1; fourteen rows) ({SP_(269, 1, "בית", "שמאי", "אומרים")} "the school of Shammai say"; {SP_(269, 1, "אלא", "אם", "כן", "מצא", "בה", "ערוה")} "unless he found lewdness in her"; {SP_(269, 1, "ובית", "הלל", "אומרים")} "and the school of Hillel say"; {SP_(269, 1, "אפלו", "הקדיחה", "תבשילו")} "even if she burnt his dish"): THE GROUNDS OF DIVORCE — Gittin 9:10 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — the PARAMETER Scripture leaves open (the design\'s DV24-01; 254:3\'s same phrase read at the camp). Fresh.')
srow(269, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'HILLEL\'S SCHOOL TO SHAMMAI\'S: IF "THING" IS SAID WHY "UNSEEMLINESS", IF "UNSEEMLINESS" WHY "THING"? WITHOUT "UNSEEMLINESS" — SHE WHO GOES OUT FOR A THING MIGHT REMARRY AND SHE WHO GOES OUT FOR LEWDNESS NOT; WITHOUT "THING" — FOR LEWDNESS SHE GOES OUT, FOR A THING NOT. ({SP_(269, 2, "אם", "נאמר", "דבר", "למה", "נאמר", "ערות")} "if \'thing\' is said why is \'unseemliness\' said?"; {SP_(269, 2, "היוצאה", "מפני", "דבר")} "she who goes out for a thing"; {SP_(269, 2, "מפני", "ערוה", "תצא")} "for lewdness she goes out"): the two words each a clause — the ground and the remarriage; Hillel\'s reading of the pair. Fresh.')
srow(269, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA: EVEN IF HE FOUND ANOTHER FAIRER THAN SHE — "IF SHE FINDS NO FAVOR IN HIS EYES". ({SP_(269, 3, "אפלו", "מצא", "אחרת", "נאה", "הימנה")} "even if he found another fairer than she"): the third opinion of Gittin 9:10 — the ground the husband\'s eyes alone. Fresh.')
srow(269, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE WRITES FOR HER" — FOR HER NAME; HENCE: ANY BILL NOT WRITTEN FOR THE WOMAN\'S NAME IS INVALID. HOW? HE WAS PASSING IN THE MARKET — ETC., THE MISHNAH. ({SP_(269, 4, "לשמה")} "for her name"; {SP_(269, 4, "כל", "גט", "שנכתב", "שלא", "לשם", "אשה", "פסול")} "any bill not written for a woman\'s name is invalid"): THE MISHNAH CITED BY ABBREVIATION IN THE HEBREW ("etc., the Mishnah" — Gittin 3:1, the scribes\' copy; RUN 1\'s 228:8 the precedent) — the bill\'s WRITING an effect with the name its parameter (the design). Fresh.')
srow(269, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"WRITES" — ONLY IN INK? WITH PIGMENT, RED OCHRE, GUM OR VITRIOL WHENCE? "WRITES" — WITH ANYTHING. ({SP_(269, 5, "כתב", "בדיו")} "wrote in ink"; {SP_(269, 5, "בסם", "ובסיקרא", "בקומוס", "ובקנקנתום", "מנין")} "with pigment, red ochre, gum or vitriol — whence?"): the ink\'s class unbounded (Gittin 2:3\'s list, the English\'s Tosefta). Fresh.')
srow(269, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"A DOCUMENT" — ONLY A SCROLL? ON LEAVES OF REED, NUT, OLIVE, CAROB WHENCE? "HE GIVES" — ANYTHING; WHY "DOCUMENT"? AS A SCROLL LASTS, SO ANYTHING LASTING; R. JUDAH B. BETEIRA: AS A SCROLL IS DETACHED FROM THE GROUND, SO ANYTHING DETACHED. ({SP_(269, 6, "עלי", "קנים", "עלי", "אגוז")} "on reed leaves, on nut leaves"; {SP_(269, 6, "של", "קימא")} "of permanence"; {SP_(269, 6, "תלוש", "מן", "הקרקע")} "detached from the ground"): the surface\'s class by prototype — two predicates disputed (Gittin 2:4 the English\'s "cf."). Fresh.')
srow(269, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"CUTTING OFF" — THAT IT BE A CUTTING OFF: "ON CONDITION YOU NEVER GO TO YOUR FATHER\'S HOUSE" — NO CUTTING OFF; "FOR THIRTY DAYS" — A CUTTING OFF. "PERMITTED TO EVERY MAN BUT SO-AND-SO" — R. ELIEZER PERMITS, THE SAGES FORBID; AFTER HIS DEATH FOUR ELDERS ENTERED TO ANSWER HIM. ({SP_(269, 7, "שיהא", "כריתות")} "that it be a cutting off"; {SP_(269, 7, "שלא", "תלכי", "לבית", "אביך", "לעולם")} "that you never go to your father\'s house"; {SP_(269, 7, "אין", "זה", "כריתות")} "this is no cutting off"; {SP_(269, 7, "מתרת", "לכל", "אדם", "אלא", "לפלוני")} "permitted to every man but So-and-so"; {SP_(269, 7, "רבי", "אליעזר", "מתיר", "וחכמים", "אוסרים")} "R. Eliezer permits and the sages forbid"; {SP_(269, 7, "נכנסו", "ארבעה", "זקנים")} "four elders entered"): THE BILL\'S DEFINITION — a bond that ends; a lasting condition no divorce, a thirty-day one a divorce (a CLOCK); Gittin 9:1 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "="). Fresh.')
srow(269, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'R. TARFON ANSWERED: SHE MARRIED HIS BROTHER, WHO DIED CHILDLESS — HOW DOES SHE CONTRACT THE LEVIRATE? HE STIPULATED AGAINST WHAT IS WRITTEN IN THE TORAH, AND SUCH A CONDITION IS VOID — SO IT WAS NO CUTTING OFF. ({SP_(269, 8, "נענה", "רבי", "טרפון")} "R. Tarfon answered"; {SP_(269, 8, "היאך", "מתיבמת")} "how does she contract the levirate?"; {SP_(269, 8, "וכל", "המתנה", "על", "מה", "שכתוב", "בתורה", "תנאו", "בטל")} "whoever stipulates against what is written in the Torah, his condition is void"): THE RULE OF THE VOID CONDITION named in the spine (Ketubot 9:1, Bava Metzia 7:11 the English\'s "//") — 25:5\'s levirate inside chapter 24 as the test case. Fresh.')
srow(269, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: WHERE DO WE FIND IN THE TORAH ONE PERMITTED TO ONE MAN AND FORBIDDEN TO ANOTHER? PERMITTED TO ONE, PERMITTED TO ALL; FORBIDDEN TO ONE, FORBIDDEN TO ALL — NO CUTTING OFF. ({SP_(269, 9, "היכן", "מצינו", "בתורה")} "where do we find in the Torah"; {SP_(269, 9, "שמתרת", "לאחד", "ואסורה", "לאחר")} "that she is permitted to one and forbidden to another"): the status indivisible — a woman\'s marital state one value for all men. Fresh.')
srow(269, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELAZAR B. AZARIAH: "CUTTING OFF" — A THING THAT CUTS BETWEEN HIM AND HER; R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: I SEE R. ELAZAR\'S WORDS. ({SP_(269, 10, "דבר", "הכורת", "בינו", "לבינה")} "a thing that cuts between him and her"; {SP_(269, 10, "רואה", "אני", "את", "דברי")} "I see the words of"): the definition by the word\'s root — the bond severed whole; the third elder\'s answer preferred. Fresh.')
srow(269, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA: IN WHICH WAS THE TORAH STRICTER, THE DIVORCEE OR THE WIDOW? THE DIVORCEE IS GRAVER; IF THE LIGHTER WIDOW IS FORBIDDEN TO ONE PERMITTED HER (THE LEVIR\'S BOND), THE GRAVER DIVORCEE ALL THE MORE TO ONE FORBIDDEN HER — NO CUTTING OFF. ({SP_(269, 11, "במה", "החמירה", "תורה")} "in which was the Torah stricter?"; {SP_(269, 11, "חמורה", "גרושה", "מאלמנה")} "the divorcee is graver than the widow"): the fourth elder\'s a fortiori — the levirate widow the lighter case, the ranking of two statuses. Fresh.')
srow(269, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: SHE MARRIED THE ONE (SO-AND-SO), BORE HIM SONS, HE DIED, SHE MARRIED ANOTHER — ARE NOT THE FIRST ONE\'S SONS MAMZERIM? NO CUTTING OFF. ({SP_(269, 12, "לא", "נמצאו", "בניו", "של", "ראשון", "ממזרים")} "are not the first one\'s sons mamzerim?"): 248\'s status (the mamzer) the consequence of a flawed bill — the divorce cell and the assembly cell joined by the child. Fresh.')
srow(269, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN HER HAND" — ONLY HER HAND? HER ROOF, HER COURTYARD, HER RUIN WHENCE? "HE GIVES" — ANYWHERE; WHY "HAND"? AS HER HAND IS HER DOMAIN, SO ANYTHING THAT IS HER DOMAIN. ({SP_(269, 13, "לרבות", "גגה", "חצרה", "וחרבתה")} "to include her roof, her courtyard and her ruin"; {SP_(269, 13, "שהיא", "רשותה")} "which is her domain"): THE HAND IS THE DOMAIN — the delivery\'s parameter by prototype (Gittin 8:1 the answer sheet). Fresh.')
srow(269, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'"GIVES IT IN HER HAND AND SENDS HER FROM HIS HOUSE" — ONCE HE GIVES IT HE SENDS HER; HENCE: HE WHO THROWS A BILL TO HIS WIFE IN HER HOUSE OR HER COURTYARD — SHE IS DIVORCED, ETC., THE MISHNAH; "TAKE IN THIS BOND OF DEBT", OR SHE FOUND IT BEHIND HIM — ETC., THE MISHNAH. ({SP_(269, 14, "כיון", "שנותנו", "בידה", "משלחה", "מביתו")} "once he gives it in her hand he sends her from his house"; {SP_(269, 14, "הזורק", "גט", "לאשתו")} "he who throws a bill to his wife"; {SP_(269, 14, "הרי", "זו", "מגרשת")} "she is divorced"; {SP_(269, 14, "כנסי", "שטר", "חוב", "זה")} "take in this bond of debt"): THE MISHNAH BY ABBREVIATION TWICE in one row (Gittin 8:1-2 — the English supplies the omitted text in braces): the delivery\'s cases the answer sheet\'s; the headless piska\'s last row. Fresh.')
srow(270, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SHE GOES OUT OF HIS HOUSE" (24:2) — THE WOMAN GOES OUT FROM BEFORE THE MAN. The head row of piska 270 ({SP_(270, 1, "שהאשה", "יוצאה", "מלפני", "האיש")} "the woman goes out from before the man"): the direction of the divorce — his house, her going. Fresh.')
srow(270, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND GOES AND BECOMES ANOTHER MAN\'S" — THAT SHE NOT MARRY IN HIS NEIGHBORHOOD. ({SP_(270, 2, "שלא", "תנשא", "עמו", "בשכונה")} "that she not marry in his neighborhood"): a PLACE parameter of the remarriage. Fresh.')
srow(270, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"ANOTHER" — THE TORAH ALREADY CALLED HIM "OTHER". ({SP_(270, 3, "כבר", "קראתו", "התורה", "אחר")} "the Torah already called him \'other\'"): the second husband named by the word — a homily on the noun. Fresh.')
srow(270, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THE LATTER MAN HATES HER" (24:3) — SCRIPTURE INFORMS YOU THAT YOU WILL COME TO HATE HER. ({SP_(270, 4, "הכתוב", "מבשרך")} "Scripture informs you"; {SP_(270, 4, "עתיד", "לשנאתה")} "will come to hate her"): the verse read as a forecast — 24:3 carries no head, its rows inside 270. Fresh.')
srow(270, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"OR THE LATTER MAN DIES" — SCRIPTURE INFORMS YOU THAT SHE WILL BURY HIM. ({SP_(270, 5, "שעתידה", "לקברו")} "she will bury him"): the second forecast. Fresh.')
srow(270, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY A DIVORCEE? THE WIDOW WHENCE? "OR THE LATTER MAN DIES"; IF THE WIDOW IS INCLUDED WHY "DIVORCEE"? THE WIDOW IS PERMITTED TO THE LEVIR, THE DIVORCEE FORBIDDEN. ({SP_(270, 6, "אלמנה", "מנין")} "the widow — whence?"; {SP_(270, 6, "אלמנה", "מתרת", "ליבם", "גרושה", "אסורה", "ליבם")} "the widow permitted to the levir, the divorcee forbidden to the levir"): the two ways the second marriage ends, and the levirate\'s bar on the divorced — chapter 25\'s law read into 24:3-4 a second time (269:8). Fresh.')
srow(270, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT ONE WHO MISCONDUCTED HERSELF AFTER HER DIVORCE BE FORBIDDEN TO RETURN? "HE WRITES HER A BILL … AND SHE GOES OUT" — SHE WHO GOES OUT BY A BILL IS FORBIDDEN TO RETURN, NOT SHE WHO MISCONDUCTED HERSELF. ({SP_(270, 7, "שקלקלה", "על", "בעלה")} "who misconducted herself against her husband"; {SP_(270, 7, "היוצאה", "בגט", "תהא", "אסורה", "לחזור", "לו")} "she who goes out by a bill is forbidden to return to him"): the bar\'s trigger the second marriage, not misconduct — the status "forbidden to return" set by 24:2\'s "becomes another\'s". Fresh.')
srow(270, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT ONE WHO GIVES A BILL TO HIS LEVIRATE WIDOW MAY NOT TAKE HER BACK? "HER FIRST HUSBAND MAY NOT" (24:4). WHENCE THAT A WOMAN WHOSE HUSBAND WENT OVER THE SEA, WHO WAS TOLD "YOUR HUSBAND IS DEAD" AND REMARRIED, AND HE CAME BACK — GOES OUT FROM BOTH AND NEEDS A BILL FROM BOTH? "HER FIRST HUSBAND MAY NOT TAKE BACK THE ONE HE SENT". ({SP_(270, 8, "לנותן", "גט", "ליבמתו")} "one who gives a bill to his levirate widow"; {SP_(270, 8, "למדינת", "הים")} "to a land over the sea"; {SP_(270, 8, "שתצא", "מזה", "ומזה")} "she goes out from this one and that one"; {SP_(270, 8, "וצריכה", "גט", "מזה", "ומזה")} "and needs a bill from this one and that one"): Yevamot 10:1 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — the husband over the sea, the walk\'s case of a false death report; THE ROW THE DUMPS COUNTED AMONG CHAPTER 25\'S (the English\'s "Dt.25:5-10" for the rite of the shoe (chalitzah, the loosening); the Hebrew cites 24:4). Fresh.')
srow(270, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHOM HE SENT AWAY" — ONLY FROM MARRIAGE TO MARRIAGE? FROM BETROTHAL TO BETROTHAL, BETROTHAL TO MARRIAGE, MARRIAGE TO BETROTHAL WHENCE? "HER FIRST HUSBAND MAY NOT TAKE THE ONE HE SENT". ({SP_(270, 9, "מן", "הנשואים", "לנשואים")} "from marriage to marriage"; {SP_(270, 9, "מן", "הארוסים", "לארוסים")} "from betrothal to betrothal"): the four transitions — betrothal a state the bar covers. Fresh.')
srow(270, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE B. KIPPAR IN R. ELAZAR B. AZARIAH\'S NAME: FROM BETROTHAL PERMITTED, FROM MARRIAGE FORBIDDEN — "AFTER SHE WAS DEFILED"; THE SAGES: BOTH FORBIDDEN; THEN WHY "AFTER SHE WAS DEFILED"? TO INCLUDE THE SOTAH WHO SECLUDED HERSELF. ({SP_(270, 10, "מן", "הארוסים", "מתרת")} "from betrothal permitted"; {SP_(270, 10, "מן", "הנשואים", "אסורה")} "from marriage forbidden"; {SP_(270, 10, "לרבות", "סוטה", "שנסתרה")} "to include the suspected wife who secluded herself"): the disputed parameter; Numbers 5\'s sotah (the tape\'s own daemon) barred to her husband by 24:4\'s word — a CALL edge to be taught (the compile). Fresh.')
srow(270, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'SO JEREMIAH 3:1 SAYS: "IF A MAN SENDS AWAY HIS WIFE AND SHE GOES FROM HIM". ({SP_(270, 11, "הן", "ישלח", "איש", "את", "אשתו")} "if a man sends away his wife"): THE PROPHETS\' RECEIPT OF 24:1-4 — Jeremiah cites the law as known ("shall he return to her again?"), the run citation ahead for the compile\'s readback. Fresh.')
srow(270, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR SHE IS AN ABOMINATION" — R. JUDAH: SHE IS AN ABOMINATION, HER CHILD IS NOT. ({SP_(270, 12, "היא", "תועבה", "ואין", "הולד", "תועבה")} "she is an abomination but the child is not an abomination"): the child of the forbidden return NO MAMZER — the abomination formula (find 5) on the woman alone; 24:4 carries no head. Fresh.')
srow(270, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND MAKE NOT THE LAND SIN" — TO WARN THE COURT ABOUT IT. ({SP_(270, 13, "להזהיר", "בית", "דין", "על", "כך")} "to warn the court about it"): the court\'s arm — the land\'s sin the court\'s failure to bar the return (Onkelos: "make not the land liable"). Fresh.')
